        <mxCell id="caption" value="&lt;b&gt;Fig. 1. Overall framework of PairSelect.&lt;/b&gt; We insert a training-free token selection module after the middle layer of a pre-trained video&lt;br&gt;Transformer encoder. Tokens are grouped into spatially adjacent pairs, and the token with larger L₂ norm is kept in each pair, followed by a group-wise&lt;br&gt;quota to achieve the desired compression ratio. The selected tokens are fed into the remaining encoder blocks and the frozen detection head to predict&lt;br&gt;video-level anomaly scores." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=23;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#111111;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="52" y="879" width="1440" height="108" />
        </mxCell>
